IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crp-dates`
IMPORT `crp-rules`
IMPORT `crp-seat`

-- Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA) -- cases for the claimant's questions (crp-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text (with Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 O. 18A and
-- Interpretation Act 1984 ss 61, 62), with the section, and never copied from the encoding's output. Day counts and
-- weekdays are worked in the comments (1 March 2026 is a Sunday). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the claimant in a class action`

§§ `ss 2, 4, 6, 10 -- can the claim be in a class action`

-- Order: day commenced, claimants (counting me), shared circumstances, substantial common issue, cross-vesting only.
-- Part 2 came into operation on 25 March 2023 (compilation table); the day before, only Part 1 (fork F1, finding 1).
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 25 3 2023) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 24 3 2023) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 14 9 2022) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(1): before Part 1 came into operation, a scope limit with no "only".
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 13 9 2022) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 24 3 2023) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 500 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6(1)(a): "7 or more persons".
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6(1)(b), (c).
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 10.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 7, O. 18A r. 2 -- standing`

-- Order: as above, then sufficient interest of my own, acting by a lawyer.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1) is silent on a person without a sufficient interest of their own.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- O. 18A r. 2: no lawyer, no.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6 fails: a no, whatever the standing.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 6 2025) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 24 3 2023) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(3); a substituted representative is outside its words (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

