#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 28 2 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 2 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 32 -- my limitation period`

-- Began 1 March 2026; old last day 31 March 2026: 30 days left (2-31 March).
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `the class action is still going` (`the day` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `my limitation period is suspended`
-- Opted out 10 May 2026: 10 May + 30 days = 9 June 2026.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 9 6 2026)
-- Ended without disposing of my claim 1 July 2027: + 30 days = 31 July 2027.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `the class action and its appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim` (`the day` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 31 7 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `my claim was finally disposed of` (`the day` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` FALSE (`the day` 31 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `section 32 does not reach my claim`
-- Old last day before the class action began: nothing left to suspend.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 28 2 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
-- Class action begun on the old last day: no days left after it; the period runs again on the opt-out day only (fork F13).
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 1 3 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 10 5 2026)

