§§ `s 28 -- the fund`

-- Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b): the 6 months begin the day after the order; s 62(3): they end on the corresponding date
-- less one, or on the last day of the month where there is no corresponding date (fork F10).
-- Order 15 Jan 2026: begins 16 Jan; 16 Jul less one = 15 Jul 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 15 7 2026
-- Order 31 Aug 2025: begins 1 Sep; 1 Mar 2026 less one = 28 Feb 2026. Order 31 Aug 2027: 29 Feb 2028 (leap year).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `the day` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `the day` 29 2 2028
-- Order 30 Aug 2025: begins 31 Aug; no 31 Feb, so the last day of February: 28 Feb 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 30 8 2025) EQUALS `the day` 28 2 2026
-- Order 28 Aug 2027: begins 29 Aug; 29 Feb 2028 exists, less one = 28 Feb 2028. Order 29 Aug 2027: begins 30 Aug; no
-- 30 Feb, so 29 Feb 2028.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 28 8 2027) EQUALS `the day` 28 2 2028
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 29 8 2027) EQUALS `the day` 29 2 2028
-- Order 31 Dec 2025: begins 1 Jan 2026; 1 Jul less one = 30 Jun 2026. Order 30 Jun 2026: begins 1 Jul; 1 Jan 2027 less
-- one = 31 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 31 12 2025) EQUALS `the day` 30 6 2026
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 12 2026
-- Order 30 Nov 2026: begins 1 Dec; 1 Jun 2027 less one = 31 May 2027 (not 30 May: fork F10).
#ASSERT `What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` (`the day` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 5 2027
-- Order 1 Feb 2026, period ending 1 Sep 2026. On the last day: in the period.
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- One day late: only under s 28(4).
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 2 9 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 2 9 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 2 9 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before the fund order: not within the period, and not after its end.
#ASSERT `Can I claim from the fund?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 31 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The rule itself (s 28(3)(c)), run over a claim on the last day of the period and on the day after.
-- 1 Feb to 1 Sep 2026: 28+31+30+31+30+31+31 = 212 days.
#ASSERT `days from` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) EQUALS 212
#ASSERT `s 28(3)(c) -- my claim was in the period` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3)(c) -- my claim was in the period` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 9 2026) (`the day` 2 9 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#TRACE `s 28(3)(c) -- my claim in the distribution period` 212 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the group member` DOES `make a claim for payment out of the fund` AT 212

§§ `s 30(3) -- appeal by a group member`

-- Representative's last day Mon 30 Mar 2026; + 21 days = Mon 20 Apr 2026.
#ASSERT `By when can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 20 4 2026
-- Fri 27 Mar 2026; + 21 = Fri 17 Apr 2026.
#ASSERT `By when can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 17 4 2026
-- Sat 28 Mar 2026; + 21 = Sat 18 Apr 2026, an excluded day: Mon 20 Apr 2026 (s 61(1)(e)). Sun 29 Mar: Sun 19 Apr: Mon 20 Apr.
#ASSERT `By when can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 28 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 20 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 29 3 2026) EQUALS `the day` 20 4 2026
-- Window after Fri 27 Mar 2026: 28 Mar to 17 Apr 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 28 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 17 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 18 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 27 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The representative appealed in time; I am not in the group.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (`the day` 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 27 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 1 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Weekend roll-over: representative's last day Sat 28 Mar 2026; filing Mon 20 Apr is in time, Tue 21 Apr is not.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 28 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal for the group?` (`the day` 28 3 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 21 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 36 -- maintenance and champerty`

-- s 36 came into operation 25 March 2023 (compilation table); "accrued before the day" saves only earlier causes.
#ASSERT `Can I be sued for maintenance or champerty?` (`the day` 25 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be sued for maintenance or champerty?` (`the day` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be sued for maintenance or champerty?` (`the day` 24 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
